A||N||7||kornholio||how did you mount your amps?||||1||
Z||000000||kornholio||10-05-2000||11:42 PM||||Does anyone have pics of where they mounted their amps?  I was going to mount my amp behind the passenger seat but wasn't sure of a few things:<P>1. Do I need a piece of wood under my amp, or can I just mount it to the carpeted board as long it is secure?<P>2. Where's the best spot to ground the amp if mounted in this location?<P>3. Where's a good spot to drill a hole for the power wire?||||reg||1
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||10-05-2000||11:55 PM||||I mounted mine behind the passenger seat. I just drilled four holes and mounted it over the carpeted pad. I then drilled a hole inboard of the amp location for my power wire. You have to be sure that you don't drill into anything important on the firewall. For a ground wire placement I grounded my amp to the same ground point as the ECM under the center console. Everything seems to work just fine...Good Luck||||reg||7
Z||000002||Oreif||10-06-2000||01:36 AM||||My power wire is just under the battery mount. As for ground I used the bolt for the passeger side seat rail. I put a 1/4" peice of plywood under the carpet and mounted amp on top of the carpet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||10-06-2000||02:52 AM||||two tiny amps sound stream used to make in a small computer type brief case that sits in my front trunk. power runs through fire wall by battery, along pass. side and goes into front trunk under right side dash. ground connected to bolt in front trunk.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gkozlov||10-06-2000||07:30 AM||||Click on my signiture to go to my website and then go to my audio page there are some pictures of my alpine F306 and Fosgate Punch 40 mounted behind the pass side seat.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||10-06-2000||08:12 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out_2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out_2.jpg</A>     I dynamated a 1/2" thick piece of PARAPLY (birch plywood) to the fire wall and screwed the amps to them. through the carpet. and had my 2ga. wire and all my RCAs under the carpet. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||william_thorniii||10-06-2000||09:18 AM||||Friends,<P>For those of you fortunate/unfortunate enough to be running automatic transmissions have a factory installed power acces hole.  There are two large (2"x4" approximately) access holes for transmission cabling with grommets in the center of the firewall directly behind the ecm.  The top one on cars equipt with an auto is not used for any cabling/linkage.  I simply pushed my amp wire through that point, then up under the fake firewall carpeting and out right at my amp.  <P>I also used the seatbelt shoulder bolt to ground my amp.  <P>William T. Thorn, III ||||reg||3
Z||000007||Formula||10-06-2000||06:27 PM||||I used the "factory power access hole but had to drill it out so the wire would fit.  Then I grounded it to the chasis right by the battery, there are already several factory grounds there... the amp is mounted on the fake firewall||||reg||1
